// Auto-generated caption module for Stage 4f Consensus-Meta42 Responder & Patient Exemplar Radar Figures

#let caption_meta42_responder_radar = [
  *Pan-cancer `Consensus-Meta42` 12-spoke radar immunogram across out-of-fold classifier predictions, empirical `RECIST` outcomes, $2 times 2$ stromal-gating regimes, and 12-marker sub-simplex percentage shares ($N = 1,015$ patients).*
  *(a)* Out-of-fold (`5 times 5` repeated stratified CV, $ell_2$-penalized logistic regression) classifier-predicted Responder (`Predicted R`, $n = 437$, blue circle polygon) versus Non-Responder (`Predicted NR`, $n = 578$, vermilion square polygon) radar profiles across $K = 12$ compartment-balanced `Consensus-Meta42` marker states (`M13`, `M15`, `M34`, `M14`, `M37`, `M29` on the right effector-humoral hemisphere $0 degree .. 150 degree$; `M23`, `M17`, `M19`, `M21`, `M26`, `M12` on the left stromal-suppressive barrier hemisphere $180 degree .. 330 degree$). Radial coordinates represent unsupervised within-trial standardized Aitchison centered log-ratios (`CLR z-score`, mean $plus.minus 95%$ CI) relative to the dashed $z = 0$ cohort-parity circle.
  *(b)* Empirical clinical `RECIST v1.1` Responder (`Observed R`, `CR/PR`, $n = 319$) versus Non-Responder (`Observed NR`, `SD/PD`, $n = 696$) radar profiles across the 9 CRI-iAtlas trials; spoke asterisks denote Benjamini–Hochberg-adjusted two-sided Welch $t$-test false discovery rates (`**` $q < 0.01$, `***` $q < 0.001$; all 12 spokes significant at $q_("BH") <= 0.0033$).
  *(c)* Zero-leakage `5`-fold out-of-fold $2 times 2$ stromal-gating corner regimes evaluated on unblended raw `InstaPrism` `Consensus-Meta42` fractions: `High-R / Permissive` (`ORR` $= 51.6%, n = 128$, teal circle) expands strongly across `M37` `TLS B` ($+1.09$ SD), `M13` `Tex` ($+1.00$ SD), and `M14` `M1-TAM` ($+0.87$ SD) while retracting on `M23` `Mat. CAF` ($-1.04$ SD), whereas `High-R / Excluded` (`ORR` $= 27.6%, n = 98$, purple triangle) co-expands collagen-crosslinking `M17: ISLR+COL5A2+ myCAF` ($+0.25$ SD) alongside `M37` `TLS B` ($+0.35$ SD) and `M13` `Tex` ($+0.16$ SD), illustrating desmoplastic myofibroblast exclusion of pre-existing anti-tumor immunity.
  *(d)* Direct 12-marker re-closed sub-simplex percentage shares ($tilde(theta)_(i, k) = 100% dot theta_(i, k) \/ sum_(m in cal(M)_(12)) theta_(i, m)$, summing to $100.0%$ per patient; vertical dashed line marks $1\/12 = 8.33%$ uniform parity) comparing `Pred. R`, `Pred. NR`, `Obs. R (CR/PR)`, and `Obs. NR (SD/PD)` means ($plus.minus 95%$ CI) alongside DerSimonian–Laird `Pan-iAtlas-Meta` random-effects deconvolution coefficients $hat(beta)_("meta")$.
]

#let caption_meta42_patient_exemplars_radar = [
  *Individual patient-level `Consensus-Meta42` 12-spoke radar immunograms contrasting two representative checkpoint responders (`CR`/`PR`) and two primary-resistant non-responders (`PD`) across solid-tumor histologies.*
  Each panel displays an individual patient's within-trial standardized compositional `CLR z-score` polygon ($z in [-2.5, +2.5]$ around the dashed $z = 0$ trial-parity ring) overlaid on the corresponding pan-cancer empirical `RECIST` reference centroid (`Observed R Mean (CR/PR)` or `Observed NR Mean (SD/PD)`, slate dashed polygon), annotated with out-of-fold predicted responder probability $hat(P)_("OOF")(R)$, overall survival (`OS`), and 12-marker sub-simplex share partitioning between the 6-state Responder Effector-Humoral Pole and the 6-state Non-Responder Stromal-Suppressive Barrier Pole.
  *(a) Responder Exemplar 1 (`Liu_Sample137`, Metastatic Melanoma, `RECIST CR`, `High-R / Permissive`)*: Achieves complete response (`OS` $= 25.4$ months, censored; $hat(P)_("OOF")(R) = 0.86$) with simultaneous multi-lineage expansion across all six effector-humoral spokes (`M29` `Plasma` $z = +2.33$, `M13` `Tex` $+2.16$, `M37` `TLS B` $+1.96$, `M14` `M1-TAM` $+1.78$, `M15` `Stem CD8` $+1.59$, `M34` `Tem CD8` $+1.51$; Responder Pole sub-simplex share $= 67.6%$) and deep contraction of all six barrier spokes (`M12` `Hypox.` $-2.26$, `M23` `Mat. CAF` $-2.13$, `M21` `Treg` $-1.92$; Barrier Pole share $= 32.4%$).
  *(b) Responder Exemplar 2 (`IMvigor210 #10239`, Urothelial Bladder Cancer, `RECIST PR`, `High-R / Permissive`)*: Achieves durable partial response (`OS` $= 18.7$ months, censored; $hat(P)_("OOF")(R) = 0.84$) driven by coordinated humoral-effector infiltration (`M29` `Plasma` $z = +2.74$, `M13` `Tex` $+2.26$, `M14` `M1-TAM` $+1.92$, `M37` `TLS B` $+1.92$, `M15` `Stem CD8` $+1.79$, `M34` `Tem CD8` $+1.53$; Responder Pole share $= 66.5%$) and absence of mesenchymal/stromal barriers (`M26` `EMT` $-2.24$, `M23` `Mat. CAF` $-1.96$; Barrier Pole share $= 33.5%$).
  *(c) Non-Responder Exemplar 1 (`Hugo_Pt10`, Metastatic Melanoma, `RECIST PD`, `Low-R / Excluded`)*: Exhibits primary progressive disease ($hat(P)_("OOF")(R) = 0.26$) characterized by severe left-hemisphere expansion across mesenchymal, regulatory, myeloid-suppressive, and desmoplastic CAF states (`M26` `EMT` $z = +2.17$, `M21` `Treg` $+2.09$, `M19` `MDSC` $+1.99$, `M23` `Mat. CAF` $+1.95$, `M12` `Hypox.` $+1.58$, `M17` `myCAF` $+1.54$; Barrier Pole share $= 67.9%$) and collapse of right-hemisphere adaptive/innate effectors (`M14` `M1-TAM` $-2.24$, `M15` `Stem CD8` $-2.16$, `M34` `Tem CD8` $-2.00$, `M13` `Tex` $-1.98$; Responder Pole share $= 32.1%$).
  *(d) Non-Responder Exemplar 2 (`IMmotion150 #p01492`, Clear-Cell Renal Cell Carcinoma, `RECIST PD`, `Low-R / Excluded`)*: Exhibits primary progressive disease ($hat(P)_("OOF")(R) = 0.18$) dominated by stromal-myeloid-mesenchymal barrier states (`M26` `EMT` $z = +1.79$, `M21` `Treg` $+1.77$, `M23` `Mat. CAF` $+1.64$, `M19` `MDSC` $+1.62$, `M17` `myCAF` $+1.51$; Barrier Pole share $= 63.7%$) with concomitant depletion of tumor-reactive `M13` `Tex` ($-2.01$), `M15` `Stem CD8` ($-1.55$), and `M34` `Tem CD8` ($-1.54$; Responder Pole share $= 36.3%$).
]
